- **Side activity:** paying a worker through their **ИП** on a special regime changes nothing — one ТК 27 feature makes it employment, payroll included.
- There is **no general 4% self-employed rate**. The four 1% contributions (ОПВ, ОПВР, СО, ВОСМС) apply only to performers working **through internet platforms**, withheld by the operator (СК ст. 102-1 пп. 2–4; ОСМС ст. 28), and ИПН inside that regime is **0%** (НК ст. 720 п. 1). Off-platform, the ordinary rates apply.
- **AIFC:** RK nationals enrol in their RK pension scheme (s 63); foreign staff of qualifying participants are ИПН-exempt until 01.01.2066 (КЗ-МФЦА 6(6)).

## Foreign Workers & Permit Coupling
- **Constitutional scope reaches a foreign worker:** Конституция РК ст. 24 confers the labour rights on «каждый» — free labour (24(1)), safe conditions and non-discriminatory pay (24(2)), labour disputes and strike (24(3)), rest, with the working-time and leave guarantees attaching to «работающим по трудовому договору» (24(4)) — and ст. 12 п. 4 extends to foreigners and stateless persons the rights established for citizens «если иное не предусмотрено Конституцией, законами и международными договорами». That reservation is where the permit regime lives: the right is the worker's, but lawful access to the post runs through the ТК, МЗ and Приказ № 279, so argue the constitutional right and the statutory permit as two separate layers.
- **The LEO permit belongs to the employer; two narrower routes belong to the worker.** ТК 26(1)(4) bars hiring a foreigner temporarily in the RK before the employer holds the LEO's **разрешение на привлечение иностранной рабочей силы** — unless the worker holds a **справка о соответствии квалификации для самостоятельного трудоустройства** or a **разрешение трудовому иммигранту**, the two worker-held alternatives the same subparagraph names; a permit-linked contract may be fixed-term (ТК 30(1)(6)); ст. 60 подпункт 3) ТК РК ties termination to a contract made without it — note that art. 60 has **no numbered пункты** at all, so "ТК 60(1)(3)" expands to a paragraph that does not exist; the shorthand is ТК 60(3).
- Quota set and distributed by the migration authority (МЗ 11(4)) as a share of the labour force — LEO permits, countries of origin, labour immigrants (МЗ 36-1(4),(5)). **2026: 0.3% / 2.85%** (Приказ 12.12.2025 № 397 as amended 24.04.2026 by Приказ № 153). The consolidated page carries only the current redaction, so no superseded figure is quoted here. The LEO issues within its quota (Приказ № 279 пп.16–17); validity п. 25 has **four** bands, and only two of them bar extension: category 1 (heads) one, two or three years **with an extension of one, two or three years**; categories 2 and 3 twelve months **extendable by twelve months up to three times**; category 4 twelve months **without extension**; seasonal workers up to 90, 180, 270 or 365 calendar days **without extension**.
- **Внутрикорпоративный перевод:** free of charge under **п. 44** — not п. 22, which is the provision that *imposes* the fee; ≤ 3 years plus one 12-month extension, resting first on **МЗ ст. 37-3 п. 1** with Приказ № 279 п. 75 as the repeating rule; ≥ 1 year service at the transferring WTO-member entity (п. 46); **outside the annual quota** (МЗ 36-1(3)) yet permit-bound (МЗ 37-3).
- **No-permit list МЗ 36-1(2)**, 9 categories: autonomous education organisations, state bodies, priority-investment and large-SEZ staff, permanent residents, heads of foreign branches, and **graduate-level managers and specialists of the "Астана Хаб" cluster fund or its participants**.
- **AIFC is not on it** — its exemption is constitutional: participants and bodies engage foreigners **without any permit** (КЗ-МФЦА 8(1)) against high-qualification documents (8(2)); visas to 5 years (7(2)).
- **The worker's own clock is a question, not a rule.** Three parts, and only two have answers. (1) A new post cannot start early: ТК 26(1)(4) bars the contract until the new employer holds the LEO permit **or** the worker holds a справка о соответствии квалификации для самостоятельного трудоустройства or a разрешение трудовому иммигранту — the справка running 3 months, extensible to the contract term up to 3 years (МЗ 37-2(1),(3)); Приказ № 279 п. 41-1 makes the employer-side bar absolute. (2) Working meanwhile costs the worker 25 МРП, up to 10 days' arrest or expulsion (КоАП 517(5)), 15 days' arrest with expulsion on repetition (517(7)), and the employer 30–700 МРП by size (КоАП 519(1)), with the overstay ladder in 517(3)–(4) running from the stay term, not the dismissal. (3) **Unresolved, and the law is what leaves it so: how long the worker has.** Dismissal is not a ground for the permit to end (Приказ № 279 п. 41); the departure duty on permit termination is the employer's (МЗ 36-1(6)); the worker's own duty is only to leave before the visa or РВП expires or to extend it (МЗ 6(4)), and that РВП rested on the contract (МЗ 6-1 подпункт 2)). Once the ground is gone, ПП РК 21.01.2012 № 148, Правила въезда и пребывания, п. 35 says the stay «сокращается», and п. 36 leaves the decision to the МВД **without stating any period**. So ask the МВД what window it allows in the case at hand instead of quoting a figure. Astana Hub entry and work are referred by МЗ ст. 6 п. 1 to **Закон РК от 10.06.2014 № 207-V "Об инновационном кластере "Астана Хаб""**.

## Dispute Procedure: Forum, Deadlines, Burden of Proof
- **Согласительная комиссия: a mandatory pre-court stage** for most employers; courts take only unresolved issues or non-execution of its decision (ТК 159(1),(7)). Permanent parity body deciding within **15 working days** of registration (159(2),(5)). Not required in microbusiness, NPOs or foreign branches and representative offices "с численностью работников не более пятнадцати человек", in domestic work, or for executive-body officers (159(1)) — the statute does not settle whether that headcount qualifies all three organisational forms or only the last, so do not choose a reading for it. The second part of ТК 159(1) also excludes military, special-state, law-enforcement and civil-protection staff and civil servants.
- Deadlines ТК 160 — commission: **1 month** for reinstatement from delivery of the termination order, **1 year** otherwise from knowledge of the breach; court after a commission decision **2 months**; commission-bypassing claimants, as written, **3 months** / 1 year.
- **Two 2026 Constitutional Court rulings override that text.** НП КС РК 08.06.2026 **№ 81-НП**: the one-year bar does not reach unpaid wages and other mandatory payments — general **3-year** limitation, ст. 178 ГК РК. НП КС РК 12.06.2026 **№ 88-НП**: the 3-month deadline for commission-bypassing reinstatement claims is unconstitutional, so **1 year** governs.
- Remedies: reinstatement (161(2), immediately enforceable, extra pay for delay); **wages for the whole вынужденный прогул, capped at 6 months** (161(1)). **Moral damages are not in ТК 161** — the claim rests on ГК РК (особенная часть) ст. 951 and ст. 952: money compensation, fault-based (951(2)), independent of the property award (952(3)), and ст. 952 п. 2 names «лишение работы» among the factors; but ст. 951 п. 4 bars moral damages for a breach of purely property rights unless a legislative act says otherwise, so a bare wage-arrears claim carries no moral-harm head.
- **Burden of proof: the ТК carries no shifting provision** — the consolidated Code contains no burden-of-proof rule at all, so the general civil rule governs: each party proves the circumstances it relies on (ГПК РК ст. 72, a single unnumbered paragraph, in the redaction of Закон РК 29.06.2020 № 351-VI); the ГПК adds no labour-specific exception. In practice the employer justifies the ground — reasoning only.
- **AIFC forum:** EmpReg disputes go to the **AIFC Court** (s 4(3)), outside the RK judicial system and applying AIFC law (КЗ-МФЦА 13(2),(6)), with **exclusive jurisdiction** over disputes between participants, bodies and/or **their foreign employees**, AIFC-law operations and referrals by agreement (13(4)). Gap: 13(4)(1) says *foreign* employees, so for an RK national the route rests on s 4(3). **No conciliation stage and no limitation period in EmpReg** — its only dispute provision is s 4(3), and s 11(k) merely makes the employer's own grievance procedure a mandatory contract term. The gap closes inside the AIFC, never from the ТК: AIFC Court Regulations 2017 s 36 bars a proceeding «more than 6 years after the date of the events that gave rise to the proceedings» «subject to any other AIFC Regulation», and EmpReg sets no shorter period, so an AIFC employment claim has **6 years** and no mandatory pre-court stage — s 25 only has the Court *encourage* ADR, with an unreasonable refusal reflected in costs. Never quote ТК 159 or ТК 160 at an AIFC employee. **Enforcement inside the RK needs no recognition stage:** КЗ-МФЦА 13(8) has AIFC Court judgments executed «в том же порядке и на тех же условиях, что и исполнение судебных актов судов Республики Казахстан», against a Kazakh or Russian translation, appellate judgments being final and binding on all (13(7)); Закон «Об исполнительном производстве» 02.04.2010 № 261-IV lists an исполнительный лист issued on an AIFC Court decision as an enforcement document in its own right (ст. 9 п. 1 подпункт 1-1)), separately from the foreign-judgment line (подпункт 3)), with a 3-year presentation period (ст. 11 п. 1 подпункт 1-1)) and 1 year for an interim-relief приказ. So the claimant goes from the AIFC Court straight to a судебный исполнитель — no exequatur in an RK court.

## Non-Waivable Rights & Void Clauses
- **ТК 10(2) is the anchor:** terms of agreements, collective and employment contracts **and employer acts** worsening the employee's position against labour legislation are **invalid and not applied** — a signed waiver of ТК 131 severance or ТК 53 notice is ineffective. No unilateral change (ТК 10(3)); same ban for collective agreements (157(3)); discrimination prohibited (ТК 6(2),(4)).
- **AIFC has its own voidness rule**: EmpReg s 7(1) — "a provision in an agreement to waive or exclude any of those requirements is void unless expressly permitted under these Regulations". s 65 still caps termination compensation at EmpReg, Board rules and contract, so the comparator is EmpReg, not ТК. Unlike ТК 10(2), s 7(2)–(3) carve out a written settlement agreement.

## Common Pitfalls
1. Citing **Закон "О занятости населения" № 482-V** — repealed by СК № 224-VII from 01.07.2023; permits now rest on МЗ and Приказ № 279.
2. Giving a dismissed worker 3 months to sue — НП КС № 88-НП (12.06.2026) voided that.
3. Treating the согласительная комиссия as optional (ТК 159(1)).
4. Claiming Kazakhstan bans non-competes, or that compensation is mandatory — see ТК 29.
5. Inventing a probation-exempt list — ТК 36 has none, bar seasonal work (ТК 134(3)).
6. Promising AIFC staff a statutory gratuity — the current s 64 is contractual.
7. Collapsing the permit exemptions: Astana Hub in МЗ 36-1(2), the AIFC in КЗ-МФЦА 8(1).
8. Assuming an ИП contract escapes employment law (ТК 27).

## Citation Format
Expand the shorthand when answering: `ТК n(m)` = `ст. n п. m ТК РК`; `СК`, `МЗ`, `КЗ-МФЦА`, `s n(m)` likewise for the instruments in Primary Sources. Orders: `Приказ <body> от DD.MM.YYYY № N (МЮ № NNNNN)`; `НП КС РК от DD.MM.YYYY № N-НП`. Never cite ТК РК for an AIFC employee; name the regime, date every figure.

